\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{2}(1-v+{v}^{2})}{{x}^{2}({v}^{2}+1)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{1-v+{v}^{2}}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1-v+{v}^{2}}{{v}^{2}+1}-v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1-v+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}-v}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1-2v+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{1-2v+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322714 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322715 13194139534960 true] [17592186322714 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322716 13194139534960 true] [17592186322714 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322717 13194139534960 true] [17592186322714 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322718 13194139534960 true] [17592186322714 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322719 13194139534960 true] [17592186322714 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534960 true] [17592186322714 1041 "selection" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322714 1104 #edb/ref 17592186322717 13194139534960 true] [17592186322714 1110 #uuid "a13ff3d7-c434-5801-8915-f8f36749bcd0" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322715 1034 "\\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{1-v-{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322715 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534960 true] [17592186322715 1111 #uuid "1ff69b2f-8ab9-55fc-95ac-e06055ef4cb1" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322716 1034 "\\frac{1-3v-4{v}^{2}}{1+{v}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=x" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322716 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534960 true] [17592186322716 1111 #uuid "4f6536c1-66ff-5a00-a09b-46708deaac9d" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322717 1034 "\\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{1-2v+{v}^{2}-{v}^{3}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322717 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534960 true] [17592186322717 1111 #uuid "08d5a410-9b73-5792-80be-c96b14a09b04" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322718 1034 "\\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{1+v+4{v}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x}" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322718 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534960 true] [17592186322718 1111 #uuid "dc0ed936-8649-5ea2-b4a6-d868e8720314" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322719 1034 "\\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{1-3v-4{v}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322719 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534960 true] [17592186322719 1111 #uuid "5402799d-4127-507b-bcf5-4fc4e363902b" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322720 1017 #edb/ref 17592186322721 13194139534960 true] [17592186322720 1089 "q-14319" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322720 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534960 true] [17592186322720 1100 "Which of the following is a first-order homogeneous ordinary differential equation?" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322720 1113 #uuid "2c7b784c-55b7-51ac-a3da-61aa471e2821" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322720 1145 "A first-order ordinary differential equation that is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y)\n$$\n\nis said to be homogeneous if it satisfies the following property:\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty)=f(x,y)\\,\n$$\n\nThe only option in which this is the case is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2}}{{y}^{3}+{x}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nWe can check this using one of two methods.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nLet $f(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2}}{{y}^{3}+{x}^{3}}.$\n\nWe see that both the numerator and denominator are homogeneous polynomials of degree $3.$ Therefore, $f(x,y)$ is a homogeneous function of degree $3-3=0.$\n\nHence, the original differential equation is homogeneous.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo check this in detail using the definition, we first write:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2}}{{y}^{3}+{x}^{3}}\n$$\n\nWe can check that this is homogeneous showing that $f(tx,ty)=f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty) & =\\frac{(tx)^{3}-3(tx)^{2}(ty)+(tx)(ty)^{2}}{(ty)^{3}+(tx)^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{3}({x}^{3})-{t}^{3}(3{x}^{2}y)+{t}^{3}(x{y}^{2})}{{t}^{3}{y}^{3}+{t}^{3}{x}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{3}({x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2})}{{t}^{3}({y}^{3}+{x}^{3})} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2}}{{y}^{3}+{x}^{3}} \\\\  & =f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(tx,ty)=f(x,y),$ the original differential equation is homogeneous." 13194139534960 true] [17592186322721 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322722 13194139534960 true] [17592186322721 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322723 13194139534960 true] [17592186322721 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322724 13194139534960 true] [17592186322721 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322725 13194139534960 true] [17592186322721 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322726 13194139534960 true] [17592186322721 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534960 true] [17592186322721 1041 "selection" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322721 1104 #edb/ref 17592186322724 13194139534960 true] [17592186322721 1110 #uuid "8c463f5e-1065-59e9-86e1-409018d6e4fc" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322722 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{3}-3xy+xy}{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322722 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534960 true] [17592186322722 1111 #uuid "09e4268c-79a8-54aa-bf1c-aab521c18684" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322723 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{2}-x{y}^{2}+{y}^{2}}{1+{x}^{2}}" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322723 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534960 true] [17592186322723 1111 #uuid "e1974ae0-b2e1-56f8-bc06-da719dacb176" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322724 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}y+x{y}^{2}}{{y}^{3}+{x}^{3}}" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322724 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534960 true] [17592186322724 1111 #uuid "ccf0814b-0865-5a1a-a668-05f9e03eed36" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322725 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}x-{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}}" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322725 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534960 true] [17592186322725 1111 #uuid "fd40ea91-b19a-5d61-9f5e-778cf9724345" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322726 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{3}-{x}^{2}y+{x}^{3}}{{y}^{3}+1}" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322726 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534960 true] [17592186322726 1111 #uuid "b8d94ee0-0dc8-5284-8414-c6c540b932aa" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322727 1017 #edb/ref 17592186322728 13194139534960 true] [17592186322727 1089 "q-14321" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322727 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534960 true] [17592186322727 1100 "Find the general solution of the following differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{3}+x{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}y+{x}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}y}\n$$" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322727 1113 #uuid "8b60ebca-2ed3-5d6e-85d9-d8b6f959696f" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322727 1145 "This is a homogeneous equation because it is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y),\n$$\n\nand we notice that all terms in the numerator and denominator of $f(x,y)$ are of order $3$ (i.e., they are cubic).\n\nUsing the transformation $y=v(x)x$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(x) \\\\  & =x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the differential equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{y}^{3}+x{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}y+{x}^{3}}{x{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}y} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{(vx)^{3}+x(vx)^{2}+{x}^{2}(vx)+{x}^{3}}{x(vx)^{2}+{x}^{2}(vx)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{x}^{3}({v}^{3}+{v}^{2}+v+1)}{{x}^{3}({v}^{2}+v)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{v}^{3}+{v}^{2}+v+1}{{v}^{2}+v} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{v}^{3}+{v}^{2}+v+1}{{v}^{2}+v}-v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{v}^{3}+{v}^{2}+v+1-{v}^{3}-{v}^{2}}{{v}^{2}+v} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{v+1}{v(v+1)} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{v} \\\\ v\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int v\\,\\text{d}v & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}}{2} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+{C}_{1} \\\\ {v}^{2} & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2{C}_{1} \\\\ {v}^{2} & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we introduced $C=2{C}_{1}.$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}\\,.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above into our solution, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}} & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={x}^{2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C)\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322728 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322729 13194139534960 true] [17592186322728 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322730 13194139534960 true] [17592186322728 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322731 13194139534960 true] [17592186322728 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322732 13194139534960 true] [17592186322728 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322733 13194139534960 true] [17592186322728 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534960 true] [17592186322728 1041 "selection" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322728 1104 #edb/ref 17592186322732 13194139534960 true] [17592186322728 1110 #uuid "48afae7e-3aa4-57ac-a63d-e10bb01637bf" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322729 1034 "{y}^{2}={x}^{2}(-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C)" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322729 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534960 true] [17592186322729 1111 #uuid "83f2d7f8-3ad1-5422-8b19-31f60a1b04e7" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322730 1034 "{y}^{2}=x(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C)" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322730 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534960 true] [17592186322730 1111 #uuid "bd39ad16-01f7-5d31-ab99-35997a1884f4" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322731 1034 "{y}^{2}={x}^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|)+C" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322731 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534960 true] [17592186322731 1111 #uuid "bc633487-0bf1-5aa3-b454-99e596fa52f9" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322732 1034 "{y}^{2}={x}^{2}(2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+C)" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322732 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534960 true] [17592186322732 1111 #uuid "b3e39a35-fedc-5e18-94c9-09f375e9c478" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322733 1034 "{y}^{2}=x(-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|)+C" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322733 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534960 true] [17592186322733 1111 #uuid "4c862b7a-63f1-5bcc-a1c8-4288fd52a801" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322734 1017 #edb/ref 17592186322735 13194139534960 true] [17592186322734 1089 "q-8369" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322734 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534960 true] [17592186322734 1100 "Which of the following is a first-order homogeneous ordinary differential equation?" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322734 1113 #uuid "29260781-8760-5b93-aff1-74357dc9fb2c" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322734 1145 "A first-order ordinary differential equation that is written in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(x,y)\n$$\n\nis said to be homogeneous if it satisfies the following property:\n\n$$\nf(tx,ty)=f(x,y)\\,\n$$\n\nThe only option in which this is the case is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nWe can check this using one of two methods.\n\n**Method 1**\n\nLet $f(x,y)=\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}}.$\n\nWe see that both the numerator and denominator are homogeneous polynomials of degree $2.$ Therefore, $f(x,y)$ is a homogeneous function of degree $2-2=0.$\n\nHence, the original differential equation is homogeneous.\n\n**Method 2**\n\nTo check this in detail using the definition, we first write:\n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}}\n$$\n\nWe can check that this is homogeneous showing that $f(tx,ty)=f(x,y),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(tx,ty) & =\\frac{(ty)^{2}-(tx)^{2}}{(ty)^{2}+(tx)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}{y}^{2}-{t}^{2}{x}^{2}}{{t}^{2}{y}^{2}+{t}^{2}{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}({y}^{2}-{x}^{2})}{{t}^{2}({y}^{2}+{x}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =f(x,y)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $f(tx,ty)=f(x,y),$ the original differential equation is homogeneous." 13194139534960 true] [17592186322735 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322736 13194139534960 true] [17592186322735 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322737 13194139534960 true] [17592186322735 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322738 13194139534960 true] [17592186322735 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322739 13194139534960 true] [17592186322735 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322740 13194139534960 true] [17592186322735 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534960 true] [17592186322735 1041 "selection" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322735 1104 #edb/ref 17592186322738 13194139534960 true] [17592186322735 1110 #uuid "242eec18-5d8e-59e6-aba1-35057e4c3f5d" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322736 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}+x}" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322736 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534960 true] [17592186322736 1111 #uuid "14ca282c-37e1-59ec-8fd7-c4cbe5347936" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322737 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}-x}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}}" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322737 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534960 true] [17592186322737 1111 #uuid "442138ad-837f-5e1c-bec0-3f41d04a9e51" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322738 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}}" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322738 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534960 true] [17592186322738 1111 #uuid "d697354e-8a56-58da-96c2-3635505d969f" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322739 1034 "\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{y-{x}^{2}}{{y}^{2}+{x}^{2}}" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322739 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534960 true] [17592186322739 1111 #uuid "190f4372-c897-5083-a24e-307e