\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{v}^{3}{x}^{3}}{({v}^{2}+1){x}^{3}} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}+v & =\\frac{{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{v}^{3}}{{v}^{2}+1}-v \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{v}^{3}-{v}^{3}-v}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ x\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{v}{{v}^{2}+1} \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIntegrating both sides with respect to $x$, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{v}^{2}+1}{v}\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int (v+\\frac{1}{v})\\,\\text{d}v & =-\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{v}^{2}}{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|v| & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+{C}_{1} \\\\ {v}^{2}+2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|v| & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+2{C}_{1} \\\\ {v}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({v}^{2}) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we introduced $C=2{C}_{1}.$\n\nFrom the transformation $y=vx$, we get\n\n$$\nv=\\frac{y}{x}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting the above into our solution, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{y}{x})}^{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡{(\\frac{y}{x})}^{2} & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})+C \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})+C \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2})-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})+C \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}) & =C \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{x}^{2}} & =C-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}) \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{C-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2})} & ={x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534960 true] [17592186322762 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322763 13194139534960 true] [17592186322762 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322764 13194139534960 true] [17592186322762 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322765 13194139534960 true] [17592186322762 1000 #edb/ref 17592186322766 13194139534960 true] [17592186322762 10